# Production vs consumption

data solar = month,Produced,Consumed,Net; Jan,3120,7940,-4820; Feb,4080,7410,-3330; Mar,5960,7020,-1060; Apr,7340,6650,690; May,8810,6480,2330; Jun,9470,7210,2260; Jul,9620,7860,1760; Aug,8730,7590,1140; Sep,6890,6720,170

chart line solar x=month y=Produced,Consumed unit=kWh title="Solar production and consumption by month"

# Monthly detail

table solar cols=month,Produced,Consumed,Net title="Monthly detail, net is produced minus consumed"

Surplus months, where production exceeded consumption, are **Apr, May, Jun, Jul, Aug and Sep**. January, February and March were net consumers.

# Notes

The inverter was down for 4 days in March. That outage is the main reason March shows the lowest production of the spring months.

! The board will vote on adding battery storage on 2026-11-12.
